{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1414285-a-new-node-and-a-recently-arrived-technocracy-chronicle-advice-needed","id":1414285,"title":"A new Node and a recently arrived Technocracy - Chronicle Advice needed","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-09-17T16:20:27-07:00","id":1414285,"title":"A new Node and a recently arrived Technocracy - Chronicle Advice needed","content":"Hi. As usual, I come here for advice. <br /> <br /> My chronicle is set in the 1940s, based around a multi-traditional Chantry trapped between their own political infighting and the arrival of the Technocracy (which didnt exist in the country before the time the story is set in). The Chantry was built over a VERY powerful node, but its Quintessence is slowly running dry (something kept in secret by the most powerful mages there). Last session, the players discovered Tass in a salt mine 2 hours away from the city. The Tass is shaped like salt crystal. They informed people in the chantry about it. <br /> <br /> Now, what do I want to achieve with that plotline?<br /> <br /> 1. To introduce the Technocracy. Basically, the few Union agents living in the country learnt about the Tass and want to take control of the mine through a Syndicate mining company. <br /> 2. To show the players some flaws The Chantry does have thanks to their lack of union. Im thinking about a couple Cabals trying to seize the mine on their own (no joint action)...and probably clashing with each other. <br /> <br /> Any ideas for developing this would be highly appreciated (specially ideas to flesh out possible clashes between mages and mages, or mages and techs).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-17T17:21:15-07:00","id":1414296,"title":"","content":"For point 1, what's the mineral rights law in the nation where the salt mine is located? If the salt mine has a poor title, the Syndicate could try claiming it using mundane methods first before going and having to show their hand. Like in the TV show<i> Angel</i>, where the evil law firm, Wolfram and Hart, had a lawyer filing building code violations on Angel's place of business, hitting someone with bureaucracy can be really annoying. Maybe a few layers of thugs as well if a Syndicate member wants to have an organized crime group seem to be interested in the salt mine.<br /> <br /> On point 2, who are the cabals in the and why would the other cabals jump to take the Node?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-17T20:48:49-07:00","id":1414325,"title":"","content":"1. In the 1940s salt mines were property of the State. The National Bank was in charge of them, to be precise. I dont think they ran the day to day exploitation, so probably they let private companies do it, granting that as concession. If its not the case, I can say it was in my story lol.<br /> <br /> 2. Every mage in the Chantry has the right to a fixed amount of Quintessence per week, according to their rank. The node it is built on is big, but the only one mages in the region know about...until now. This unclaimed node could be a) an extra source of Quintessence for whoever claims it, and b) a symbol of prestige and &quot;fuck your ranks limitation&quot;; in other words, hubris.<br /> <br /> Initially I would have a Chorister cabal and a Verbena cabal going after the node. The other ones dont have the human-power to claim it, or are just too busy to do it.<br /> <br /> To add more context or flavor:<br /> I forgot to mention, but theres a strong catholic cult among the miners. They venerate an advocation of virgin mary, who, they think, protects them through their perilous task. They carved a small chapel into the mine and in 1950, an ultra-conservative government will build a CATHEDRAL inside the mine (real life history, btw).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","user":"Argonot","date":". 09-17-2020, 11:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-09T22:06:30-07:00","id":1417514,"title":"","content":"1. Introducing the Technocracy. Some reasons why they would show up and how they would integrate into the local community.<br /> - A Sleeper from this setting awoke into the technocratic paradigm or that of a convention (Progenitor fighting disease and malnutrition, ItX Time Motion Manager wanting to build manufacturing). By some mystical means, a mentor made contact and taught the ways of the convention. Other Union Mages heard about this and came to support him or her in advancing an agenda of prosperity through technological development. Knowing it is Trad controlled, they bring some front line people; Operatives, Enforcers, Biomechanics. The newly awakened Technocrat is from the setting and helps them integrate. <br /> - The Void Engineers' Earth Frontiers Division came to explore natural features. Others, like the Syndicate, followed. They buy influence, rather than taking any interest in the local culture. They use force to assist police against a longstanding criminal gang, gaining support this way. <br /> - A device I'm using in my current chronicle: There is no room for advancement within a particular Construct. A tech Mage leaves to carve out territory for herself. In my own chronicle, there is an informal peace treaty between factions that establishes a particular city as Trad territory. A single Progenitor mage has set up shop (a biotech startup) in the Trad controlled city. The players have the choice to tolerate her presence and maintain her as contact, capture her for interrogation or otherwise punish her for participating in an operation that affected Sleeper friends of one of the PCs. This forces the cabal to decide whether loyalty to un-awakened friends takes priority over positioning within Mage Society.<br /> <br /> 2. Here is where you have to look at how much dramatic payoff or player enjoyment you get out of the work you invest in making NPCs. One of the things that Satyros Brocato, a co-creator of the original Mage game, talked about on Mage The Podcast was the importance of ordinary Sleepers in a chronicle. He was discussing Gods and Monsters, which features templates and generation methods for different kinds of Sleepers as important characters. If the players belong to a chantry of Mages in Tradition controlled territory, are they able to simply speak to any member of the chantry? If so, you might run into a couple of problems. First, you might find it exhausting trying to give each one of these NPCs a worthwhile acting performance with memorable and unique social traits. Second, when it comes to internal conflict between &quot;a couple of cabals&quot;, every single Mage has a unique Sphere-set that you have to keep track of. Can Mage-A read Mage-B's mind without being detected by Mage-C. Are chantry members collecting fallen hairs from the PCs to better target them with Magick later? Can secret conversations that happened in the past be seen from the present using Time2? Did one of the conspirators use Time4 to ward against Time-sight? The more Mage NPCs who can be readily socially accessed by the players, the more social and Magickal intricacies you have to consider. <br /> <br /> The more you focus your efforts on Sleeper characters, the better sense of the culture and politics of the setting your players will get. Have the various cabals' agendas play out over wide geographic areas that present the players with the real concerns of citizens. It's up to the players whether they want to help a government official with a problem, in exchange for blocking the Technocracy's permit application, or just Mind him. Part of the horror aspect of the game is the players' ability to use Magick to coerce Sleepers, instead of relating to them on a human level, causing them to gradually lose their connection to the rest of humanity. Use one of your chantry NPCs to illustrate what can happen when you lose your humanity. Make them monstrous. Or have a Syndicate Mage who orders fresh new clones from FACADE every so often whose only role is to be a sex slave before their fabricated memories unwind under the stress of their master's demands. Would the players take in the spent clones and try to rehabilitate them? If so, could one of the clones exploit the PC's sympathy to execute a planned spy operation? Make each NPC a work of art and have the creative work pay off in your chronicle over time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}